# `core.autocrlf = true` with no attributes file meant every fresh checkout on
# Windows rewrote the shell scripts to CRLF, and `sh` rejects that outright:
#
#   hardware/build/run_tb.sh: 10: set: Illegal option -
#
# The blobs were always LF; the working tree was not. It surfaced when the HLS
# rewrite merge checked `hardware/build/*.sh` out for the first time, but it was
# never specific to those files — a clone of this repo on Windows could not run
# any of them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# archive/ and references/ are frozen as found (DOC-CONVENTIONS §6). `-text`
# disables EOL conversion entirely, so they check out byte-for-byte whatever was
# committed — CRLF included, which ten of the archived scripts genuinely are.
# Normalising them would be rewriting an archive.
archive/**    -text
references/** -text
